course: dictionary
lesson: 14896
title: Changing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The prefix re- means again or back, and convert means change. So reconvert means to change something back into what it was before, or into another form again. «Sam changed 2 metres into 200 centimetres, then reconverted the answer back into metres to check it.» The word back tells you the change is being undone.
explain: Look for clues in the words around it. «The old shed was reconverted into a bedroom.» The words into a bedroom show the shed has a new use, so reconvert here means changing a building back to a use it had before, or giving it a new one. Ask yourself: is something being changed back or changed again?
explain: The word can also mean bringing a person back to a belief or religion they had left. «The club hoped to reconvert Ben, who had left years before.» The club wanted Ben to come back to what he had once belonged to. Use the check: swap in «change back», and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Reconvert means to change something back into what it was before, or into another form again.
fact: The prefix re- means again or back, and convert means change.
fact: «Reconvert» can mean changing a building or machine back to its old use.
fact: «Reconvert» can also mean bringing someone back to a belief or religion they had left.
fact: Useful phrases are «reconvert to», «reconvert into» and «reconvert back».
exercise: «Mum reconverted the photo file back into its first format.» What does reconverted mean here? | Deleted the photo for ever | *Changed back into its first form | Sent the photo to a friend | Printed the photo in colour
exercise: «The old shed was reconverted into a bedroom.» What happened to the shed? | *It was changed to a new use as a bedroom | It was moved to the top of the hill | It was painted bright red | It was knocked down to make a car park
exercise: Find and copy the part of the word reconvert that means again or back. | *re | con | ert | vert
test: «Sam changed 2 metres into 200 centimetres, then reconverted it back into metres.» What does reconverted mean? | Measured it again with a ruler | Made it twice as long | *Changed back into metres | Lost the answer
test: «The club hoped to reconvert Ben, who had left years before.» What does reconvert mean here? | *Bring him back to the club he had left | Give him a new club shirt | Make him the captain of the club | Ask him to leave the club quickly
exam: Which sentence uses reconvert correctly? | *Dad reconverted the loft back into a playroom | Dad reconverted the sunny afternoon into a song | Dad reconverted his breakfast into a loud noise | Dad reconverted the kitchen into a sad story
